The Weft is a collection of four to six adventurers that have traveled across [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. They're registered with [[Org/Althane/The Guild|The Guild]] and have completed some quests in the name of justice. Among them are [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]], [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]], [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]], [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]], and the two [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] orbs [[People/Althane/Schism|Schism]] and [[People/Althane/SeRaan|SeRaan]].

They keep a base at [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/index|the lava ruin]], where the Heart they woke as [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/Damien|Damien]] forges items out of divine energy.

Immix named them "the Left" on a broadcast across [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]], showing a wanted-poster likeness of each of them beside a dossier of their deeds, their strength and the [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]] they hold. The same broadcast reaches [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where they are known as figures of Immix's talk show, [[Divinity/Immix|the Lighthouse]], and where their looks are worn by cosplayers. Divex wears the pearl [[People/Althane/Crystal Earring|Crystal Earring]], and the Weft carry a caged [[Bestiary/Mimics|tzitzimitl]]. They freed the Kaathe [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]] and [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] from the vats of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and both now travel with them.

General [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] named them the mongrels who killed his people, broke the First House beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] the House kept, and their faces went out in flyers across [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] to be hunted down and hanged in the streets. They killed him at RC3, and the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] took his body.

All four carry the chrome of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] now: a skull implant, a subdermal piece, artificial lungs, and a port in the neck, cut in by [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]]'s own hand. They can see the Rhett and hold credit there, and they pass for denizens of that planet.
